   "say": [
    {
     "at": 0.5,
     "text": "Step 13. The wiring on the back of the panel. Two cables run from here to the carrier."
    },
    {
     "at": 7.4,
     "text": "A four pin cable goes into the can header. Can high and can low run to the screw terminal of the R P 23 50 can module. 5 volts and ground come from J 7 on the carrier. The 120 ohm termination is on at both ends."
    },
    {
     "at": 22.4,
     "text": "The heartbeat uses the twelve pin header P 3. Only two of its twelve wires are needed: ground, and I-O 28. Both go to J 3 on the carrier."
    },
    {
     "at": 31.4,
     "text": "Take the ten unused wires out of the plug. Each contact is held by a small metal tongue that sits in a window of the housing. Press the tongue down with a needle, and pull the wire out to the back, without force."
    }
   ]
